00:15:29.310 --> 00:15:32.262
product suite to manage a
true hybrid environment.

00:15:34.627 --> 00:15:35.460
WESTON HUTCHINS: Hi.

00:15:35.460 --> 00:15:36.720
My name is Weston Hutchins.

00:15:36.720 --> 00:15:39.600
And I'm a product
manager for GKE on prem.

00:15:39.600 --> 00:15:41.430
Even with more
and more workloads

00:15:41.430 --> 00:15:44.400
moving to the public
cloud, on prem software

00:15:44.400 --> 00:15:48.240
remains a necessity for many
enterprise organizations.

00:15:48.240 --> 00:15:50.010
Every enterprise
has apps that are

00:15:50.010 --> 00:15:52.790
difficult to move to the
cloud or restrictions

00:15:52.790 --> 00:15:55.460
on where sensitive
workloads can run.

00:15:55.460 --> 00:15:57.883
Many are looking for
a true hybrid story--

00:15:57.883 --> 00:16:00.050
one where they can modernize
the apps for the cloud,

00:16:00.050 --> 00:16:03.650
but continue running in
their own data center.

00:16:03.650 --> 00:16:05.420
Many companies have
looked to Kubernetes

00:16:05.420 --> 00:16:07.070
to give them a
consistent environment

00:16:07.070 --> 00:16:09.290
between on prem and cloud.

00:16:09.290 --> 00:16:12.150
But getting started with
Kubernetes is challenging.

00:16:12.150 --> 00:16:14.060
There are over 50 distributions.

00:16:14.060 --> 00:16:16.430
And choosing the right
tools to install Kubernetes

00:16:16.430 --> 00:16:18.103
can prove daunting.

00:16:18.103 --> 00:16:19.520
And then once you
get a cluster up

00:16:19.520 --> 00:16:22.400
and running, you enter the
land of day 2 operations,

00:16:22.400 --> 00:16:24.200
where you not only
need tooling, but

00:16:24.200 --> 00:16:27.110
considerable operational
expertise to manage the life

00:16:27.110 --> 00:16:29.630
cycle of a Kubernetes cluster.

00:16:29.630 --> 00:16:31.730
We find a lot of
customers that start down

00:16:31.730 --> 00:16:33.830
the route of building
their own in-house DIY

00:16:33.830 --> 00:16:36.920
tooling to manage Kubernetes
later struggled to keep

00:16:36.920 --> 00:16:39.200
that tooling up-to-date.

00:16:39.200 --> 00:16:41.910
Google's answer for hybrid
is Cloud Services Platform,

00:16:41.910 --> 00:16:45.110
a stack that takes the best of
cloud native open technologies

00:16:45.110 --> 00:16:47.360
like Kubernetes and Istio,
and lets you run them

00:16:47.360 --> 00:16:48.990
in your data center.

00:16:48.990 --> 00:16:51.560
But the key benefit of
CSP is the collection

00:16:51.560 --> 00:16:53.120
of cloud services
that integrate your

00:16:53.120 --> 00:16:57.380
on prem and cloud workloads into
a single unified experience.

00:16:57.380 --> 00:17:00.140
Services like binary
authorization for security,

00:17:00.140 --> 00:17:02.630
unified log-in and monitoring
through Stackdriver,

00:17:02.630 --> 00:17:05.540
or centralized policy management
that syncs access controls

00:17:05.540 --> 00:17:07.700
across all of your clusters.

00:17:07.700 --> 00:17:10.490
At Next '19 we'll deep dive
into the infrastructure

00:17:10.490 --> 00:17:13.609
layer for CSP GKE on-prem.

00:17:13.609 --> 00:17:16.990
GKE on-prem takes all of
the technology behind GKE

00:17:16.990 --> 00:17:20.210
and installs it on top of
VMware in your data center.

00:17:20.210 --> 00:17:22.550
Once installed, you
register your cluster

00:17:22.550 --> 00:17:25.310
with Google's cloud console
to give your administrators

00:17:25.310 --> 00:17:27.740
and developers a single
pane of glass for managing

00:17:27.740 --> 00:17:29.450
their clusters and apps.

00:17:29.450 --> 00:17:31.910
In our talk at Next we'll
take a detailed look

00:17:31.910 --> 00:17:33.870
into a real world use case.

00:17:33.870 --> 00:17:36.440
Arctiq, one of our CSP
solution providers,

00:17:36.440 --> 00:17:39.160
recently rolled out GKE on-prem
to one of their customers--

00:17:39.160 --> 00:17:42.710
Optiva, a telecommunications
services company.

00:17:42.710 --> 00:17:44.480
We'll walk through
Optiva's architecture,

00:17:44.480 --> 00:17:47.180
show how GKE on-prem integrated
with their existing tools

00:17:47.180 --> 00:17:50.450
and workflows, and gives some
tips for your own installation

00:17:50.450 --> 00:17:51.770
of GKE on-prem.

00:17:51.770 --> 00:17:53.510
Check out the breakout
session online.

00:17:53.510 --> 00:17:57.218
And we'll get you up and running
with GKE on-prem in no time.

