Nice to have you here.

00:35:35.680 --> 00:35:35.820
CHEN GOLDBERG: Hi.

00:35:35.820 --> 00:35:37.290
Thank you very much
for inviting me.

00:35:37.290 --> 00:35:38.248
RETO MEIER: Absolutely.

00:35:38.248 --> 00:35:39.960
Now, hybrid cloud
is a common strategy

00:35:39.960 --> 00:35:41.730
that businesses
look to modernize

00:35:41.730 --> 00:35:44.280
while still supporting
their current applications.

00:35:44.280 --> 00:35:47.130
How does Google Cloud approach
this particular challenge?

00:35:47.130 --> 00:35:48.630
CHEN GOLDBERG: So
first of all, it's

00:35:48.630 --> 00:35:50.940
important to understand why
customers want to modernize

00:35:50.940 --> 00:35:52.543
and what they are
looking for that.

00:35:52.543 --> 00:35:54.210
And the most important
thing is for them

00:35:54.210 --> 00:35:56.880
in order to compete they have
to increase their developer

00:35:56.880 --> 00:35:59.317
agility and help them
to be more focused.

00:35:59.317 --> 00:36:00.900
And they really want
to take advantage

00:36:00.900 --> 00:36:04.020
of the amazing capabilities
that are available in the cloud

00:36:04.020 --> 00:36:06.240
and using new cloud services.

00:36:06.240 --> 00:36:09.120
But they have to make a decision
and choice because they cannot

00:36:09.120 --> 00:36:11.362
modernize everything at once.

00:36:11.362 --> 00:36:12.570
That's one of their concerns.

00:36:12.570 --> 00:36:13.987
The second thing
is that they also

00:36:13.987 --> 00:36:16.430
have concerns from
regulations that requires

00:36:16.430 --> 00:36:18.030
them to stay on-premises.

00:36:18.030 --> 00:36:20.490
So from their perspective,
it is a reality

00:36:20.490 --> 00:36:22.350
that hybrid is here to stay.

00:36:22.350 --> 00:36:25.070
And they have to choose a
hybrid strategy in order

00:36:25.070 --> 00:36:28.350
to modernize and
advance their business.

00:36:28.350 --> 00:36:30.180
For us in Google
Cloud we understand

00:36:30.180 --> 00:36:33.600
that we need to support our
customers in their journey.

00:36:33.600 --> 00:36:35.700
And our goal is to
make sure that we

00:36:35.700 --> 00:36:39.020
help them reduce the risk
instead of increasing the risk

00:36:39.020 --> 00:36:40.380
in going through this journey.

00:36:40.380 --> 00:36:42.790
And risks are coming
in different levels.

00:36:42.790 --> 00:36:47.280
For example, not
fragmenting your talent

00:36:47.280 --> 00:36:49.890
in line to create a consistent
experience everywhere,

00:36:49.890 --> 00:36:53.910
and also really leveraging the
existing assets you have today.

00:36:53.910 --> 00:36:57.030
So not asking them to buy
new hardware, for example,

00:36:57.030 --> 00:36:59.793
but really blending in to
their existing environment.

00:36:59.793 --> 00:37:01.710
STEPHANIE WONG: And how
does this truly differ

00:37:01.710 --> 00:37:03.630
from other hybrid offerings?

00:37:03.630 --> 00:37:07.230
CHEN GOLDBERG: Google puts the
user at first in the center.

00:37:07.230 --> 00:37:10.230
And we understand
that our customers

00:37:10.230 --> 00:37:12.720
appreciate to have choice.

00:37:12.720 --> 00:37:14.610
They want to be able
to choose where they're

00:37:14.610 --> 00:37:17.068
going to deploy their workloads,
what kind of tools to use,

00:37:17.068 --> 00:37:18.630
which services to use.

00:37:18.630 --> 00:37:23.070
And our goal is to make that
possible while reducing risk.

00:37:23.070 --> 00:37:26.820
We do it by building our
platform based on open source

00:37:26.820 --> 00:37:31.650
technologies, which are ensuring
that the workers are portable

00:37:31.650 --> 00:37:33.570
and we're not locking them in.

00:37:33.570 --> 00:37:38.040
And we're also now approaching
multi-cloud strategically

00:37:38.040 --> 00:37:41.310
and giving consistent experience
wherever customers choose

00:37:41.310 --> 00:37:42.735
to deploy their workloads.

00:37:42.735 --> 00:37:43.860
RETO MEIER: That's amazing.

00:37:43.860 --> 00:37:46.020
What components make up Anthos?

00:37:46.020 --> 00:37:48.330
And how do those
components work together

00:37:48.330 --> 00:37:51.360
to provide a really integrated
approach for our customers?

00:37:51.360 --> 00:37:54.810
CHEN GOLDBERG: So Anthos
is an opinion platform

00:37:54.810 --> 00:37:56.148
managed by Google.

00:37:56.148 --> 00:37:57.690
In the foundation,
in the core of it,

00:37:57.690 --> 00:37:59.400
we are using open
source technologies

00:37:59.400 --> 00:38:04.110
originated by Google, like
Kubernetes, Istio, and Knative.

00:38:04.110 --> 00:38:06.270
But this is not sufficient
for our customer

00:38:06.270 --> 00:38:09.000
to manage their heterogenous
environments they have.

00:38:09.000 --> 00:38:13.520
On top of that, we are building
in multi-cloud, multi-cluster

00:38:13.520 --> 00:38:16.230
control plane that lets
our customers connect

00:38:16.230 --> 00:38:19.320
to all of their
environments and manage them

00:38:19.320 --> 00:38:21.600
in a consistent through
a single pane of glass.

00:38:21.600 --> 00:38:24.660
We also give them tools to
manage policies and control

00:38:24.660 --> 00:38:26.910
in all of those environments.

00:38:26.910 --> 00:38:28.470
But not everything
is containerized.

00:38:28.470 --> 00:38:32.560
And this is also about investing
with what they have today.

00:38:32.560 --> 00:38:36.210
So on top of that, we are
creating a service management

00:38:36.210 --> 00:38:38.160
platform which allows
them to connect

00:38:38.160 --> 00:38:42.010
all those services regardless
of what the compute there is.

00:38:42.010 --> 00:38:44.340
And on top of everything we
have an awesome marketplace

00:38:44.340 --> 00:38:46.980
that allows us to provide
both first quality

00:38:46.980 --> 00:38:49.890
and third-party applications
available in all

00:38:49.890 --> 00:38:51.430
of those environments.

00:38:51.430 --> 00:38:52.020
STEPHANIE WONG: So
you just mentioned

00:38:52.020 --> 00:38:54.390
investing in what our customers
are already using today.

00:38:54.390 --> 00:38:57.520
How can Anthos be used to
help them modernize in place?

00:38:57.520 --> 00:38:59.562
CHEN GOLDBERG: So what we
hear from our customers

00:38:59.562 --> 00:39:02.620
is that when they come and they
want to use new cloud services,

00:39:02.620 --> 00:39:04.470
they have first to
qualify and make sure

00:39:04.470 --> 00:39:06.960
that the cloud meets their bar.

00:39:06.960 --> 00:39:09.690
Let's say they want to
use BigQuery or even GKE.

00:39:09.690 --> 00:39:12.210
They need to go through this
specific process, usually

00:39:12.210 --> 00:39:14.730
manual process, to
make sure they can

00:39:14.730 --> 00:39:16.590
let their developers use it.

00:39:16.590 --> 00:39:19.530
With GKE On-Prem they don't
need to go through that process,

00:39:19.530 --> 00:39:22.410
because we bring this technology
into their data center.

00:39:22.410 --> 00:39:24.420
And they know it meets the bar.

00:39:24.420 --> 00:39:27.068
So that's actually the fastest
way for them to innovate.

00:39:27.068 --> 00:39:28.110
RETO MEIER: That's great.

00:39:28.110 --> 00:39:30.450
What about config
management with Anthos?

00:39:30.450 --> 00:39:33.720
How can you write multi-cluster
policies right out of the box?

00:39:33.720 --> 00:39:35.470
CHEN GOLDBERG: So
that's a great question.

00:39:35.470 --> 00:39:38.370
I think that the number
one concern that CIOs have

00:39:38.370 --> 00:39:40.500
is how they manage risk.

00:39:40.500 --> 00:39:42.150
And specifically how
can they make sure

00:39:42.150 --> 00:39:45.630
that they know who access what
resources, and making sure

00:39:45.630 --> 00:39:48.760
that they know what policies
are applied everywhere.

00:39:48.760 --> 00:39:50.830
And when you have more
and more environments,

00:39:50.830 --> 00:39:52.470
you have to build
more and more tools

00:39:52.470 --> 00:39:54.010
and have more
people manage that.

00:39:54.010 --> 00:39:56.700
So Anthos config
management allows

00:39:56.700 --> 00:39:59.830
you to manage those policies
from a centralized place.

00:39:59.830 --> 00:40:02.250
And even if by accident
or by a malicious user,

00:40:02.250 --> 00:40:04.440
someone is trying to
break that policy,

00:40:04.440 --> 00:40:07.050
automatically we will
apply that policy

00:40:07.050 --> 00:40:10.618
and bring that environment
back to be compliant.

00:40:10.618 --> 00:40:12.660
STEPHANIE WONG: So more
environments, more tools.

00:40:12.660 --> 00:40:14.940
Can you elaborate on what
we're doing to give users

00:40:14.940 --> 00:40:17.580
the visibility they need so that
they can see what's happening

00:40:17.580 --> 00:40:19.170
across all these environments?

00:40:19.170 --> 00:40:19.962
CHEN GOLDBERG: Yes.

00:40:19.962 --> 00:40:22.230
So we are leveraging
open APIs, which

00:40:22.230 --> 00:40:24.570
allows us to actually integrate
with every environment,

00:40:24.570 --> 00:40:26.460
wherever the user chooses.

00:40:26.460 --> 00:40:27.780
And we are creating tools--

00:40:27.780 --> 00:40:29.610
centralized tools--
in the control plane

00:40:29.610 --> 00:40:32.220
that gives you
signals or monitoring

00:40:32.220 --> 00:40:33.780
data from all of
those environments

00:40:33.780 --> 00:40:35.530
in a consistent way.

00:40:35.530 --> 00:40:37.830
And we're also leveraging
things like Knative.

00:40:37.830 --> 00:40:40.860
We just announced Cloud
Run is beta to give

00:40:40.860 --> 00:40:43.970
a simple and effective user
experience for developers,

00:40:43.970 --> 00:40:46.220
again, to deploy to all
of those environments.

00:40:46.220 --> 00:40:47.820
So when I think
about it, it's not

00:40:47.820 --> 00:40:49.570
about portability of workloads.

00:40:49.570 --> 00:40:52.110
But it's actually about
portability of skills.

00:40:52.110 --> 00:40:54.990
Can my developers, can
my service operators,

00:40:54.990 --> 00:40:58.482
use the same set of tools,
regardless of which environment

00:40:58.482 --> 00:40:59.190
they want to use?

00:40:59.190 --> 00:41:01.110
And by leveraging open
source technologies,

00:41:01.110 --> 00:41:02.962
this is actually possible.

00:41:02.962 --> 00:41:04.170
RETO MEIER: That's fantastic.

